cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite the original thesis when discussing this research. Cite Voteview
  separately for its source data, and include the Congress and retrieval date
  when reporting results from the refreshed research companion.
type: software
title: "Eigenpolitics: Research Companion to Eigen-Politics"
authors:
  - family-names: Chelminski
    given-names: Maximilian
abstract: >-
  A local-first interactive research companion and refreshable data pipeline
  for spectral analysis of United States Senate roll-call voting networks.
  The repository preserves the original 2026 Master's thesis and analysis
  scripts. Refreshed companion results are not an exact reproduction of the
  original thesis snapshot.
keywords:
  - spectral graph theory
  - United States Senate
  - political polarization
  - roll-call voting
  - graph Laplacian
preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: "Eigen-Politics: A Spectral Analysis of the US Senate"
  authors:
    - family-names: Chelminski
      given-names: Maximilian
  year: 2026
  thesis-type: "Master's thesis"
  institution:
    name: "Graduate School of Arts and Sciences, Quantitative Methods in the Social Sciences"
